Chapter: Dnp3

 DNP3 (Distributed Network Protocol) data-link layer, the SCADA
 workhorse for electric, water, and utility telemetry (IEEE 1815).
 A link frame is a 10-byte header block (start bytes 0x0564, length,
 control, destination, source, CRC) followed by user data carried in
 blocks of up to 16 octets, each block followed by its own CRC. All
 addresses are little-endian. Each builder returns a List Integer.

 The length field counts the control, destination, and source octets
 (5) plus the user data, but not the start bytes, the length octet
 itself, or any CRC.

Section: CRC-16/DNP

 CRC-16/DNP: reflected polynomial 0x3D65 (0xA6BC in reflected form),
 initial value 0x0000, final xor 0xFFFF. The check value over the
 ASCII string "123456789" is 0xEA82.

  dnp3-crc16 : List Integer -> Integer
  dnp3-crc16 (bs) = bit-xor (dnp3-crc-loop 0 bs 0 (list-length bs)) #FFFF

  dnp3-crc-loop : Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dnp3-crc-loop (crc) (bs) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then crc
   else dnp3-crc-loop (dnp3-crc-byte (bit-xor crc (list-at bs i)) 0) bs (i + 1) len

  dnp3-crc-byte : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dnp3-crc-byte (crc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then crc
   else if bit-and crc 1 == 1
     then dnp3-crc-byte (bit-xor (bit-shru crc 1) #A6BC) (k + 1)
     else dnp3-crc-byte (bit-shru crc 1) (k + 1)

Section: Byte Helpers

  dnp3-u16-le : Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-u16-le (v) = [bit-and v 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255]

  dnp3-crc-suffix : List Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-crc-suffix (bs) = dnp3-u16-le (dnp3-crc16 bs)

  dnp3-slice : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-slice (data) (off) (count) = dnp3-slice-loop data off count 0 []

  dnp3-slice-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-slice-loop (data) (off) (count) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= count then acc
   else dnp3-slice-loop data off count (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at data (off + i)))

Section: Control Octets

 Common primary-station control octets (DIR + PRM set, function code
 in the low nibble).

  dnp3-ctrl-reset-link : Integer = #C0
  dnp3-ctrl-test-link : Integer = #C2
  dnp3-ctrl-confirmed-data : Integer = #C3
  dnp3-ctrl-unconfirmed-data : Integer = #C4
  dnp3-ctrl-request-status : Integer = #C9

Section: Header Block

  dnp3-start-1 : Integer = #05
  dnp3-start-2 : Integer = #64

  dnp3-header : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-header (ctrl) (dest) (src) (datalen) =
   [dnp3-start-1, dnp3-start-2, 5 + datalen, ctrl] & dnp3-u16-le dest & dnp3-u16-le src

  dnp3-header-block : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-header-block (ctrl) (dest) (src) (datalen) =
   let h = dnp3-header ctrl dest src datalen
   in h & dnp3-crc-suffix h

Section: Data Blocks

 User data is split into 16-octet blocks, each followed by its own CRC.

  dnp3-data-blocks : List Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-data-blocks (data) = dnp3-data-loop data 0 (list-length data) []

  dnp3-data-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-data-loop (data) (off) (len) (acc) =
   if off >= len then acc
   else let count = if len - off < 16 then len - off else 16
   in let chunk = dnp3-slice data off count
   in dnp3-data-loop data (off + 16) len (acc & chunk & dnp3-crc-suffix chunk)

Section: Application Layer

 The application layer inside the frame: an application control octet
 (FIR, FIN, CON, UNS, and a sequence number) and a function code,
 followed by object headers. An object header names a group and
 variation and a qualifier: 0x06 selects all objects of that type,
 0x00 an 8-bit start/stop index range. Class-data reads use group 60
 with variation 1..4 for classes 0..3.

  dnp3-app-fc-read : Integer = 1
  dnp3-app-fc-write : Integer = 2
  dnp3-app-fc-select : Integer = 3
  dnp3-app-fc-operate : Integer = 4
  dnp3-app-fc-direct-operate : Integer = 5
  dnp3-app-fc-cold-restart : Integer = 13

  dnp3-app-header : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-app-header (seq) (function) = [bit-or #C0 seq, function]

  dnp3-obj-all : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-obj-all (group) (variation) = [group, variation, #06]

  dnp3-obj-range8 : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-obj-range8 (group) (variation) (start) (stop) = [group, variation, #00, start, stop]

  dnp3-read-class : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-read-class (seq) (class-variation) =
   dnp3-app-header seq dnp3-app-fc-read & dnp3-obj-all 60 class-variation

  dnp3-read-range : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-read-range (seq) (group) (variation) (start) (stop) =
   dnp3-app-header seq dnp3-app-fc-read & dnp3-obj-range8 group variation start stop

Section: Frame

  dnp3-build-frame : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  dnp3-build-frame (ctrl) (dest) (src) (data) =
   dnp3-header-block ctrl dest src (list-length data) & dnp3-data-blocks data
